r his death was appointed commander. He maintained the field for one day, but was at last slain by Yudhi- ṣṭhira). -ल्या A kind of dance (mentioned with लास्य and चलित). -Comp. -अरिः an epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira.-आहरणम्, -उद्धरणम्, -उद्धारः, -क्रिया, -शास्त्रम् extraction of thorns or splinters, or that part of surgery which relates to the extraction of extraneous matter from the body. -कण्ठः a porcupine. -कर्त्तृ a surgeon. -क्रिया the extraction of thorns or other extraneous substances lodged in the body. -पर्वन् N. of the 9th book of the Mahābhārata. -प्रोत a. pierced by an arrow. -लोमन् n. the quill of a porcupine. -हर्तृ m.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a weeder.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a surgeon.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shalya", "shalyam", "śalya", "śalyam", "शल्य"], "synonyms_slp1": ["shalya", "shalyam", "śalya", "śalyam", "Salya"]}], "salyita": [{"id": "Salyita", "headword": "शल्यित", "headword_slp1": "Salyita", "fold": "salyita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "शल्यित [śalyita], a. Pierced (as with a dart); निष्कारणपरित्याग- शल्यित U.3.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shalyita", "śalyita"], "synonyms_slp1": ["shalyita", "śalyita"]}], "salaki": [{"id": "SallakI", "headword": "शल्लकी", "headword_slp1": "SallakI", "fold": "salaki", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "शल्लकी [śallakī], 1 A porcupine.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A kind of tree (of which elephants are very fond); अभिलेढु तावदासवसुरभिरसं शल्लकी- भङ्गम् V.4.44 (v. l.); U.2.21;3.6; Māl.9.6. -Comp. -द्रवः incense.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["shallakii", "śallakī"], "synonyms_slp1": ["shallakii", "śallakī"]}], "salvaH": [{"id": "SalvaH", "headword": "शल्वः", "headword_slp1": "SalvaH", "fold": "salvaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "शल्वः [śalvḥ], N. of a country. -शल्वाः The Kṣatriyas; see शाल्व.", "gloss_language": "en"}